From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 15:19:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Probe encoder availability through PyAV instead of the
 ffmpeg binary

<details><summary>Claude's draft</summary>

Rewrite ffmpeg_test_encoder() to open the encoder via PyAV's
av.CodecContext and encode a single 256x256 frame, rather than shelling
out to the `ffmpeg` executable with an 8-second nullsrc.

Benefits:
- ~12x faster (~13 ms vs ~150 ms per probe): no process spawn and only a
  single frame is encoded. Limiting the subprocess to one frame only
  reached ~110 ms, confirming process startup dominated the old cost.
- More correct: it tests the encoders PyAV's bundled libav can actually
  open, which is what the codecs use at runtime. The old test queried a
  possibly-separate `ffmpeg` binary and could green-light an encoder
  (e.g. libx264) that PyAV then fails to create, crashing the encoder
  constructor.

Tries yuv420p then nv12 so both software and hardware (qsv/nvenc/
videotoolbox) encoders validate. Result remains memoised via lru_cache.

